 ## Overview
-Weighted Order-Independent Transparency (OIT) for 3D Gaussian Splatting computes a blended image without sorting Gaussians by depth, using a learnable weight function to approximate correct transparency blending [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard 3DGS rasterization, which requires sorting by distance to camera to correctly accumulate transmittance, by eliminating the sorting step entirely in favor of a weighted average [S1, unofficial]. The method builds on [SparseOIT Rasterizer](7562-sparseoit-rasterizer.md).
